labelHistory.evidence:
Defects demonstrated by a reproduction in the orchestrator's review round and fixed by the factory in 8d726b249182a059ae70aa9d1567c359d139621f. Original findings:
major src/pipeline/engine.ts:3400: Persist each coordinator confirmation as it completes, so a restart repeats none of them
Review checked the honest-verdict, scope, refactor and execution-safety points and found them sound. Two other reports turned out to be properties of the shared targeted retry and gate provenance that the land queue already has; they're filed separately and need no change here.

The issue asks that a restart not run the coordinator re-run twice. The confirmation loop (~src/pipeline/post-merge-confirmation.ts:38) runs every failing LAN check before anything is saved: `attempt.result` is written only after `confirmPostMerge` returns (~src/pipeline/engine.ts:3405). With two failing checks, a restart while the second confirmation runs repeats the original gates, the re-check and the completed first confirmation. Reproduced: three local executions instead of two.

Fix:
- Before the first coordinator confirmation starts, persist the comparison after the re-check, with each failing check's worker attribution, in `postMergeGates` (same sha/base/head/round scoping). A restart then resumes from it without re-running the original gates or the re-check.
- Persist each check's confirmation outcome as soon as it completes, before the next one starts.
- On resume, confirm only the checks that have no recorded outcome. A confirmation interrupted before its outcome was saved may run again.

Add this test from review (adjust helpers to fit), make it pass and don't weaken it. Also assert that after the restart the original post-merge gates and the re-check aren't executed again.

```ts
  test("restart between coordinator confirmations keeps the completed first check", async () => {
    writeFileSync(
      join(repoDir, ".limitless.toml"),
      `[gates]\nretry_files = "fake-targeted {files}"\nchecks = [{ name = "test-a", run = "fake-suite-a" }, { name = "test-b", run = "fake-suite-b" }]\n`,
    );
    await sh(
      [
        "git",
        "-c",
        "user.email=t@t",
        "-c",
        "user.name=t",
        "commit",
        "-qam",
        "interrupted confirmation fixture",
      ],
      { cwd: repoDir },
    );
    const bare = await githubFixture();
    const f = start(async (s) => {
      if (roleOf(s) === "triage") return { structured: triage({ suggested_profile: "quick" }) };
      if (roleOf(s) === "review") {
        await advanceBase(bare, "base.txt", "new base\n");
        return { structured: approve };
      }
      return { files: { "farewell.txt": "goodbye\n" } };
    });
    await f.stop();
    registerGithub(f, bare);
    const fixture = postMergeWorkerFixture(f);
    const execute = fixture.processSpy.getMockImplementation();
    if (!execute) throw new Error("Missing process mock");
    let confirmations = 0;
    fixture.processSpy.mockImplementation(async (opts) => {
      if (opts.cmd[0] === "/bin/sh" && ++confirmations === 2)
        throw new SimulatedTermination("during second coordinator confirmation");
      return execute(opts);
    });
    try {
